WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.560
Goodbye, Iron Man, hello, Ironheart?

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.590
According to a new report by We Got This Covered,
Marvel Studios may have decided which hero

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:13.260
will assume the Iron Man mantle following
Tony Stark's death in Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:18.120
The outlet cites an unnamed source that claims
the bigwigs at Marvel and Disney are planning

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.720
to have Riri Williams, also known as Ironheart,
become the new Iron Man.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.480
She is said to be scheduled to debut in the
MCU in either a Phase 4 or a Phase 5 film,

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.660
and will, quote, "have Tony's suit to help
her."

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.440
The ultimate plan for Ironheart, per We Got
This Covered's info, is to have the hero fight

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.260
alongside the New Avengers, led by Brie Larson's
Captain Marvel.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.520
For those who haven't heard of Ironheart,
here's a brief run-down on the character:

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.660
she's an introverted teenager with genius-level
intellect who was accepted to M.I.T. at age

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.160
12.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.140
Her smarts caused her to retreat into herself,
but when she reverse-engineered the Iron Man

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:59.440
Armor Model 41 suit to create her own version
of the armor, something sparked inside her.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:04.660
She wound up stepping into the suit and committing
a few acts of rogue vigilantism before Tony

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.660
Stark noticed her and endorsed her wish to
become a superhero.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.979
Ultimately, when Tony slips into a coma after
battling Captain Marvel, it's Riri who carries

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.120
on his legacy as Ironheart.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.680
We Got This Covered's report notes that "several
characters" will attempt to rise as the new

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.380
Iron Man.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:24.940
These contenders contenders include Don Cheadle's
War Machine, a close friend of Tony's, and

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:29.460
Tom Holland's Spider-Man, who saw Tony as
a father figure and trained under him to become

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.380
an Avenger during Spider-Man: Homecoming.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.540
"That's not a hug I’m just getting the door.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.320
We’re not there yet."

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:42.040
Apparently, both War Machine and Spidey soon
realize that the gig just isn't for them,

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.639
and Ironheart will go on to assume the mantle.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.200
But really, how plausible is the notion that
Ironheart will be the new Iron Man in the

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:49.700
MCU?

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.320
Well, it certainly helps that this exact thing
has happened in Marvel Comics.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:59.880
In August of 2016, WIRED exclusively confirmed
that Riri Williams would formally take the

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.900
Iron Man torch from Tony Stark during the
events of the new Invincible Iron Man #1.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:10.400
On the other hand, although We Got This Covered
does cite a source, it's not a named source.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:14.920
Anyone reading this report and choosing to
believe it or brush it off is doing so based

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.400
solely on the word of an anonymous source.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.040
Now, this isn't to say that We Got This Covered
aren't reputable.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.319
quite the opposite, actually, and the outlet
has hit the head on numerous nails in the

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:29.930
past, such as accurately reporting the Avengers:
Endgame leak that revealed the Chitauri would

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:34.120
be in the movie and reporting the news that
Robert Pattinson was in talks to become the

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.260
new Batman months before Variety confirmed
the scoop.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.540
We Got This Covered really could be dishing
the truth here, but without any corroboration

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:44.600
on that source it's just impossible to know
for sure.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.080
"Did you know?"

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:51.040
"...Yes."

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:56.340
Everything considered, this could be a legitimate
leak or just a bunch of hogwash.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:01.220
It would be seriously cool to see a new hero
take over for Tony Stark, much like Anthony

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:06.159
Mackie's Falcon is all set up to become the
new Captain America in Steve Rogers' stead,

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:10.590
and it makes a lot of sense for Ironheart
to be that person, considering what went down

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.460
in the comics.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:15.620
And yes, fans will certainly have to take
this report with a grain of salt.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:19.790
But regardless of whether Riri Williams will
be appearing on the silver screen anytime

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:24.590
soon, you can probably rest assured that Kevin
Feige and Marvel know what they're doing and

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.140
that Tony Stark's legacy is in good hands.

